# Keep build tooling and repository metadata out of any upload.
#
# wrangler.toml points [assets] at ./dist, so these should never be reachable.
# This file is a second line of defence in case the directory is ever changed
# back to "." — it costs nothing and prevents republishing the source tree.
#
# wrangler honours .wranglerignore for `wrangler deploy` asset uploads.

.git/
.github/
.wrangler/
node_modules/

src/
tools/
scripts/

README.md
README-DEPLOY.md
.wranglerignore
.gitignore
wrangler.toml
package.json
package-lock.json

*.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
